                     /note="lacO: the 17 bp core of the lac operator O1, the
                     LacI binding site of the E. coli lac promoter. Gilbert &
                     Maxam 1973 sequenced the repressor-protected fragment,
                     about 27 bp long, and published 24 bp of it:
                     TGGAATTGTGAGCGGATAACAATT. This part is an interior window
                     of that sequence; its own ends are not the ones the paper
                     reports and are unverified. The 24 bp form is annotated on
                     the catalog's Plac as 'lac operator O1', the 21 bp form on
                     Ptac and T7lac."
